From: Fabian Renn-Giles <fabian@fielding.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: qdsp6: clear stale channel_map entries

q6dma_set_channel_map() only writes the first tx_num/rx_num entries.
The per-DAI module_config in q6apm-lpass-dais is persistent, so entries
written by an earlier, wider configuration survive a later narrower one.
The codec DMA active_channels_mask is built from non-zero channel_map
entries, so stale entries can make it disagree with num_channels.

Clear the whole channel_map before filling it in both setter branches.
The default mapping path is already cleared by q6dsp_map_channels().

Fixes: c663014e452d ("ASoC: qcom: audioreach: compute active channel maps from channel_map")
Signed-off-by: Fabian Renn-Giles <fabian@fielding.dev>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5-5
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261028100708.6808-1-fabian@fielding.dev
---
Local backport draft of the two setter changes from Fabian's original
patch, on top of Zhangfei Gao's v3. The original helper hunk is superseded.
Original author and assistance trailer retained. This is not a new patch
for submission under Jesse's authorship or a claim of A16 hardware testing.

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
@@ -99,6 +99,7 @@
 				tx_num);
 			return -EINVAL;
 		}
+		memset(cfg->channel_map, 0, sizeof(cfg->channel_map));
 		for (i = 0; i < tx_num; i++)
 			cfg->channel_map[i] = tx_ch_mask[i];
 
@@ -123,6 +124,7 @@
 				rx_num);
 			return -EINVAL;
 		}
+		memset(cfg->channel_map, 0, sizeof(cfg->channel_map));
 		for (i = 0; i < rx_num; i++)
 			cfg->channel_map[i] = rx_ch_mask[i];
 
